================================

CRC filename
  CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE over every 128-byte CP/M record. The final record's
  on-disk padding is included. Output counts and checksums are hexadecimal.

CMP file1 file2
  Compare every CP/M record. Reports the first differing record/offset or
  which file is shorter. An optional A: through P: drive prefix is accepted.

MEM address [length]
  Read-only hex/ASCII memory view. Address is four hexadecimal digits;
  lengthPECTED END OF HEX FILE$INVALID SEPARATOR$NO DIRECTORY SPACE$INVALID FORMAT WITH SPARCE FILE$MAKE FILE$OPEN FILE$PRINTER BUSY$CAN'T DELETE TEMP FILE$ *5<P_lzЋќ±АРЯсь)<\fp}NO DIRECTORY SPACE$NO DATA BLOCK$CAN'T CLOSE CURRENT EXTENT$SEEK TO UNWRITTEN EXTENT$RANDOM RECORD OUT OF RANGE$RECORDS DON'T MATCH$RECORD LOCKED$INVALID FILENAME$FCB CHECKSUM$ВХгюВ2FTe$NONRECOVERABLE$R/O DISK$R/O FILE$INVALID DISK SELECT$INCOMPATIBLE MODE$INVALID PASSWORD$ALREADY EXISTS$LIMIT EXCEEDED$†‡ is two hexadecimal digits, defaults to 10h, and is capped at 40h.

WC textfile
  Count lines, words, and bytes through the CP/M text EOF byte (1Ah).
  Counts are six-digit hexadecimal values.

FIND textfile token
  Print lines containing a case-insensitive token and report the hexadecimal
  match count. The token is limited to 31 characters and lines to 120.

STRINGS filename
  Print ASCII runs of at least four characters from all physical file
  records. Unlike text tools, 1Ah is treated as an–џЁјeОЯTо	
